<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Palanpur State</h1><p class="st-meta">1370 CE – 1949 CE (approx.) · capital Palanpur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Pashtun-ruled state of northern Gujarat whose Lohani Nawabs held power for centuries, and whose Jain merchants later came to dominate the diamond trade.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The ruling Lohani family, of Afghan origin, served the sultans of the region and by tradition held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalore">Jalore</a> before establishing themselves at Palanpur. The register's start date follows family tradition; the dynasty was firmly settled at Palanpur by the 17th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Palanpur was a largely agricultural state on the border of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, under Mughal and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> influence before coming under British protection in 1817. Its Muslim Nawabs ruled a mainly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> and Jain population. The Palanpuri Jain merchant community later became leading diamond traders in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Nawab Taley Muhammad Khan acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and Palanpur merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a> in 1949. It is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banaskantha-district">Banaskantha district</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/palanpur-state.jpg" alt="Palanpur State" width="320" height="162"><figcaption>Image: Robert Alfers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Palanpur.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1370 CE – 1949 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Palanpur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Taley Muhammad Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (rulers), Hinduism, Jainism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>India</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Palanpur</dd></dl></aside></div>
